   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **%Dos Banjos** (2 other sources): Marked as a banjo duet between Billy Strings and Billy Falling [1][2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Blackberry Blossom**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **In The Baggage Coach Ahead**: back after 129 archived shows (706 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Dig A Little Deeper In The Well**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- ***I Told Them All About You**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **#Country Blues**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **^Black Clouds**: back after 69 archived shows (450 days) [4]\n- **My Little Georgia Rose**: rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **$Standing In The Need Of Prayer**: rare: 14 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2024-03-01.billys** (recommended): source not stated; 26 songs; 145 min [1]\n- **billystrings2024-03-01.billy**: source not stated; 26 songs; 146 min [2]\n- **billystrings2024-03-01**: source not stated; 26 songs; 145 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Z-Man counts this as show number 65 of 2024, from Team Dirty South and Home Team Recording [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2024-03-01.billys**: taped by David Dyche; transferred by David Dyche; source: Neumann KM 140’s > V-3 > Sound Devices 744T 24/96 [1]. Also: Recorded with Neumann KM 140 mics through a V-3 preamp into a Sound Devices 744T at 24/96, then Logic Pro, Sound Studio and xACT; David Dyche recorded and seeded this version [1]\n- **billystrings2024-03-01.billy**: taped by David Dyche; transferred by David Dyche; source: Neumann KM 150’s > Nick Active Cables > Naiant PFA’s > Sound Devices 744T 24/96 [2]. Also: Recorded with Neumann KM 150 mics, Nick active cables and Naiant PFAs into a Sound Devices 744T at 24/96, then Logic Pro, Sound Studio and xACT; David Dyche recorded and seeded this version [2]\n- **billystrings2024-03-01**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V'S>Sound Devices Mix-Pre 6 II (48/32) [3]. Also: Schoeps CCM4V mics went into a Sound Devices Mix-Pre 6 II at 48/32, then Sound Forge, CD Wave and 16-bit FLAC [3]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by scrapedknee.com: [Billy Strings – Atlanta, GA – 2024 : Scraped Knee](https://scrapedknee.com/billy-strings-atlanta-ga-2024-2/) [5]\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings 2024-03-01 State Farm Rainbow Foil - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/merch/2024-03-01-state-farm-rainbow-foil/) [6]",
